# The sha256 of Certificate/axioms.lock: the exact laws the formal model was last checked
# against. It is meant for the formal-model CI job (model/README.md, "The CI job"),
# which compares it with the lock, from the repository's root,
#     grep -v '^#' model/lock.sha256 | shasum -a 256 -c -
# and fails when they differ: on any change to the lock, since it also holds every word
# the statement of a proposition, a porism or a companion reaches. A change to the axioms
# (one added, removed or restated), or to a word an axiom reaches, sends someone back to
# the model before CI is green: to the translation (generated in Model/Laws.lean, with
# the hand translations of Model/Hand.lean and Model/Laws/), its checks in Check/, and the
# proofs in the plane of the laws that changed. A change that touches none of these, such
# as a word only a proposition's statement uses, moved into the foundations from Staging/,
# needs only this hash renewed.
# tests/model/lock.sha256 does the same for the numerical harness, and CI's model job
# checks that one.
#
# Filled in when the model package was started (18 October 2026), at the lock of main's
# f17b427. When the lock changes, bring the model up to date, then replace the line
# below with the output of
#     shasum -a 256 Certificate/axioms.lock
# run from the repository root (keep these comment lines).
#
# Renewed on 18 October 2026, with tests/model/lock.sha256, when the words of the mixed
# angles (brief 0011) joined the vocabulary: words only the companions of III.16 and III.31
# use, and no law of the model changes.
#
# Renewed on 18 October 2026, when the words of stage 3's statements (brief 0006) joined
# the vocabulary: words only the propositions and their companions reach, so none of
# the model's laws changes.
#
# Renewed on 19 October 2026, when the rule that every circle has a centre,
# Tacit.exists_centre, joined the axioms (brief 0008, section 2): the generator writes its
# law, Model/Assembly.lean gathers Euclidean.exists_centre, which proved it in the plane
# before it landed, and Check/Hand.lean compares the hand translation with the library's
# declaration. The other 87 laws and the 37 words they reach are unchanged.
#
# Renewed on 19 October 2026 for the combined vocabulary of stages 3 and mixed angles:
# 88 axioms, byte-identical to the centre-rule revision, and 120 words of vocabulary.
#
# Renewed on 19 October 2026 for brief 0008, section 7: CirclesCut joins the vocabulary,
# and TouchesInternally asks for a point within instead of distinct circles. The 87 axioms
# and all 37 words they reach are unchanged; no model law changes.
#
# Renewed on 19 October 2026 for the merged vocabulary of stage 3, mixed angles and
# brief 0008, section 7: 88 axioms, unchanged, and 121 words of vocabulary.
#
# Renewed on 19 October 2026, when eight axioms became theorems (the owner approved both
# retirements that day): their laws leave the generated translation;
# the other 79 axioms and every word are unchanged, byte for byte.
#
# Renewed on 19 October 2026, when the restricted rule of superposition (brief 0009, #75)
# replaced the existential one: the generated law, its hand translation and its proof in
# the plane were brought to it (model/README.md), and the other 86 laws are unchanged.
# Renewed on 20 October 2026 after the coincidence marker was integrated (brief 0009,
# #75): the vocabulary grows from 206 to 208 words. Coincidence and its step join
# the lock, and the three Derives congruence constructors take the marker. All 87
# axiom statements are unchanged. The marker records a step without changing its
# interpretation; the existing placement proofs and numerical law still apply.
# Renewed on 20 October 2026, when the restricted rule was merged after the first
# retirement wave: the generated translation has the 79 laws of wave one with the
# restricted superposition law and its words, and the lock's vocabulary stays at 208 words.
#
# Renewed on 21 October 2026, when 31 more axioms became theorems (the owner's decision of
# 19 October 2026), merged after the restricted rule: their laws leave the generated
# translation, and Check/ compares each hand translation with the theorem's type directly;
# the other 48 axioms and every word are unchanged, byte for byte.
#
# Renewed on 21 October 2026, when axiom wave one was merged into train C6a: the lock is
# main's 79 rules and Tacit.exists_centre, 80 axioms, with 121 words of vocabulary. The
# generator writes 80 laws, Model/Assembly.lean gathers all 80 with Euclidean.exists_centre
# among them, and the eight retired rules keep their plane proofs and audits as derived
# facts, with no field of Laws.
#
# Renewed on 21 October 2026, when main's restricted rule of superposition (#191) was
# merged into train C6a, through tooling/centre-given-meaning at 980569da: the lock is
# main's 79 axioms, with Tacit.superposition restated as Superposition.Rule primitives, and
# Tacit.exists_centre, 80 in all, with 238 words of vocabulary, main's 208 and this train's
# 30. The generator writes 80 laws, the restricted superposition law and exists_centre's
# among them, and Model/Assembly.lean gathers all 80.
#
# Renewed on 21 October 2026, when the second retirement was merged with train C6a (#240):
# the lock is the second retirement's 48 axioms and Tacit.exists_centre, 49 in all, with
# 238 words of vocabulary; it is main's lock less the 31 lines of the retired axioms, every
# other line byte for byte. The generator writes 49 laws, exists_centre's among them, and
# Model/Assembly.lean gathers all 49.
